WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.890
Japan's government debt is
over 200 per cent of its GDP.

2
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.480
You might expect lenders to
demand sky-high interest.

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.430
Yet its 10-year bond yield was held near 0

4
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.750
per cent for several years from 2016.

5
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.910
So does all that government
borrowing touch the businesses

6
00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.690
that want to borrow too?

7
00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.430
When a government borrows more,

8
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.220
can it leave firms with less to invest?

9
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.000
In this mission, you'll build
a market where the price

10
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.690
is an interest rate.

11
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:30.610
Then you'll use a graph lab:

12
00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:34.400
change government borrowing
and watch private investment.

13
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.630
Your mission: find out what government
borrowing does to the money firms can invest.
